  "name": "GM Drum Sounds — every drum, one row each",
  "description": "One row per General MIDI drum sound on channel 10 (mDrum), labelled \"midiName NotePlayed DrumName=MPL\" in each row's tooltip, e.g. \"mDrumBass C Bass Drum=m10,4(C)\". Each row plays its drum four times. Row 0 plays all 47 GM drums (B- to A+++) in order. A bank holds 36 rows, so the 12 rarer sounds (Cabasa, Maracas, Short Whistle, Long Whistle, Short Guiro, Long Guiro, Hi Wood Block, Low Wood Block, Mute Cuica, Open Cuica, Mute Triangle, Open Triangle) are only in row 0. Notes are relative to the bass drum: C is the kick (MIDI 36), D the snare, F# the closed hat, C#+ the crash. The drum each note plays depends on the kit: these are the GM names, which DLSMusicDevice and Drum Kit Designer follow.",
